From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The mirrored copies made a little a scene, before they're
 seen (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the Cycling Road the game stuttered as each new part of it came in (a
test run of 2026-11-06). Its maps are mirrored past the scenery beside
them (patch 0069), and a map's mirrored copy was made all at once as its
strip first came into the view: all its widths' lists cut (5, and the
whole map's with the rows moved over), the rows moved over cut too: 3.8 ms
on the PC as a map came in at 300,6xx, several times that on the 3DS, in
one frame.

The map is loaded before it's seen, and its copy is now made in the scenes
between, PORT_MIRROR_STEP_BYTES (48 KB) of its lists a scene, its cut
lists kept as they're made (PortMirrorCopy.cuts, .next); seen before it's
done, the rest is cut at once as before. The copies are the same. On the
PC riding south from 300,590: the copy made in 7 scenes of 0.5-0.7 ms
before it was seen (3.8 ms in one before), the pictures the same frame by
frame (an NPC under the bridge facing another way, as between any two
runs); Valley Windworks at 250,648, 246,652 and 250,660 and the Cycling
Road at 300,600, 300,640 and 300,670 the same pictures.

